A||||2||Turbo88||ECU fuel mod||||1||
Z||000000||Turbo88||08-31-2001||01:35 AM||||Hello all, I'm new to the board and wanted to say hi. I also have a question.. I'm begining the buildup of a fiero 2.8 targeting 450-500hp range. The question I have is, does anyone make a good custom chip with the correct fuel maps and reworked MAP/MAT sensor readings. If all else fails, I'm into an aftermarket FMU but I wanted to try the stock unit with reworked programing. Does anyone have any suggestions?<P>Thanks for the info..<P>Bryan||||reg||1
Z||000001||dman||08-31-2001||04:58 PM||||Hello.<P>From previous research on this subject I learned the following. Design One Systems in OK have a turbo kit for the Fiero. I believe it is a newer version of the old Miller-Woods kit. It uses the stock fiero ECM with a custom chip to support the 2-bar map sensor. Their stage 2 kit uses an ECM from an 85 fiero (6869)that has been slightly modified to support a knock sensor (The newer fiero ECMs didn't have the capability to adapt the sensor). They have a web page so you can get more info <A HREF="http://www.designonesystems.com" TARGET=_blank>www.designonesystems.com</A> <BR>Give them a call, perhaps they'll sell you a chip.<P>Another alternative you may wish to consider is to use a GM ECM that already supports boost. The ECM's found on a Sunbird Turbo, Syclone/Typhoon can be adapted to work. Of course you'll need to tweak some of the maps and probably in the case of the Sunbird a few other changes to make it work on a 6 cylinder application. Also the ECMs that were coupled to the quad four were similar (7749). I've heard you can use the Syclone program on those ECMs.<P>Lastly, the Haltech E6GM seems like an excellent alternative. Adjusting the maps won't require the old burn chip, dyno, re-burn chip cycle since you can download new maps dynamically with a laptop computer. Wiring it up is supposedly very simple, most of the wires match up, just a few wires to adjust. I believe the guys at West Coast Fieros are currently playing with such a setup on some of their newer turbo projects (3800 Series II turbo...looks like a neat project!)<P>Please keep us (or at least me) informed about your project. I'm always interested in learning more about such conversions. And of course good luck and have fun.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Turbo88||08-31-2001||05:57 PM||||Thanks for the reply.. I'm actually thinking of leaving the 2.8 where it is at around 250-260 hp and building a 3.8 ohc. Electromotive makes an ECU that will allow Sequential Fire Inejection and includes a DIS ignition controller. This ECU is adaptable and is somewhat simular to the HAL systems. <P>I'm going to start selling kits for both the 60* and the 90* engines (to help offset the cost of developement <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. <P>Thanks for the reply though, my little Formula set idle for almost 4 years and I haven't had time/money to do anything with it but I wouldn't give it up! I love beating my LS1 buddies with it!!!||||reg||1
